<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50250" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκέσ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for suppliants</i>, epith. of
			Zeus, their protector, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				616
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				484
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				345
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				929
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cos</span>); also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἱκέσιος</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				402
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thera</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς Ἱκεσίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pisc.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκεσία Θέμις Διός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					360
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of</i> or <i>consisting of suppliants</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένων ἱ. λόχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					111
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>suppliant</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκεσίους πέμπων λιτάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					495
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκεσίαν . . προστροπάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					108
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκεσίοις σὺν κλάδοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					102
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκεσίᾳ χερί</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				108
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάγκας ἱκεσίους λῦσαι</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				39
			</span></i>; of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκέσιός σε λίσσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					1230
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκεσία τε γίγνομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					710
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκέσιος, ὁ</span>, as Subst., <i>suppliant,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Berl.Sitzb.
				1927.167
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cyrene</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ἱκέσιος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμπλαστρος</span>), name of a
			<i>plaster</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.62
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ἱκεσίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.64
				</span></i>
			. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐκ-</span>, exc. metri gr. in
				<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.215
			</span></i>.]</div>
